  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want a menu on each message with the actions HFR allows (quote, edit, profile, MP, alert…), so that I act on a message as on the site.\n\n### Scope\n\nTyped bridge (decoded message enum, never page-supplied code), menu built from LOT-031 actions by a pure policy (own post, logged out, MP, locked). Each action goes to a handler protocol; actions whose handler lot is not merged are hidden. 'Link' (copy permalink) implemented here.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: high · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'typed JS bridge (C14)' and 'message action policy (C15)'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `MessagesView.swift` (`MessagePopupMenuActionKind` 13 actions, `MessagePopupMenuPolicy`, `Coordinator` `WKScriptMessageHandler`), `Classes/ObjCMessageActionsBuilder.m`; tests `HFRswiftTests/MessagePopupMenuPolicyTests.swift`\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-087-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-083 (#101, in-progress)\n- LOT-031 (#58, in-progress)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged (unblocked 2026-10-29, steward ext/opus-helper1)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- #273 (own post on a public topic: the edit link shape, and which MP, favourite and alert actions remain)\n- any other page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Capture first if you can\n\n- **CLI session with capture access** (the maintainer's Mac, LOT-001 kit): try capture #273 before the lot. It is a read-only GET of a page that already holds a post of the account.\n- **Any other session:** build the own-post rules from legacy and LOT-031, and list #273 as *pending capture* in the spec.\n- **Either way:** post one comment on review #330 saying what you did: the capture PR and fixture id, or what the policy assumes, with the legacy file:line. The capture does not block the lot (operator, 2026-10-29).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Policy ported from legacy with its tests (`MessagePopupMenuPolicyTests.swift`), including 'Link' kept as 'Link' (Bybifok PR #3 note).\n- [ ] The bridge rejects unknown message names and malformed payloads (tests).\n- [ ] Handler registry: a later lot (alert, AQ, bookmark, BL/WL, flag here, edit, delete, quote, profile, MP) plugs in without editing the policy.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).",
